  "limits": [
    {
      "id": "S1",
      "status": "RESOLVED",
      "text": "The initial reading=fst only compared readings, not raw objects. The final Inscription type is Fix(normalize), and the faithful restricted reading gives literal equality with dueObject; finite raw trajectories are expressly rejected."
    },
    {
      "id": "S2",
      "status": "RESOLVED",
      "text": "A globally injective preserved reading would force normalization to be the identity. The generic contract proves that obstruction; the concrete model uses injectivity only on the fixed locus."
    },
    {
      "id": "S3",
      "status": "RESOLVED",
      "text": "The named split_forbids_minimality lemma alone permits a zero left part. The concrete bridge now proves both matrix faces nonzero and links leftFace.mulVec to normalize, avoiding that inference."
    },
    {
      "id": "S4",
      "status": "PASS_SEMANTIC_SCOPE",
      "text": "Soundness and completeness characterize a predicate for an independently fixed reading and target. The docstrings identify the interpretation as INPUT/ONTO and its elementary logical consequences; no universal truth of the interpretation is claimed."
    },
    {
      "id": "S5",
      "status": "LIMIT",
      "text": "Normalized satisfaction holds already at n=0 and does not depend on the decay coefficient. The half-nat coefficient supplies effective dynamics and convergence, not the admissibility predicate or its truth."
    },
    {
      "id": "S6",
      "status": "LIMIT",
      "text": "normalize(0,1)=0 is a rejected control. Nonannihilation is proved for the admissible target/initial orbit, not for every input and not as a physical unattainability theorem about absolute zero."
    },
    {
      "id": "S7",
      "status": "PASS_SEMANTIC_SCOPE",
      "text": "Idempotence and preservation of reading are distinct obligations. Ledger independence is explicitly reused as definitional, not offered as extra physical evidence."
    }
  ],
